1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,691
The water cycle describes how water moves continuously around the Earth. First,

2
00:00:04,691 --> 00:00:10,202
evaporation: the Sun heats water in oceans, lakes and rivers, and it turns into water vapour,

3
00:00:10,202 --> 00:00:11,668
which rises into the air.

4
00:00:12,727 --> 00:00:18,180
Next, condensation: as water vapour rises, it cools and changes into tiny droplets of water,

5
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:19,880
which collect to form clouds.

6
00:00:20,939 --> 00:00:25,981
As droplets grow larger and heavier, they fall as precipitation, such as rain or snow.

7
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:32,141
Water then flows across the land as run-off, and collects in rivers, lakes and oceans.

8
00:00:32,141 --> 00:00:37,184
Some soaks into the ground to become groundwater, which can also flow back to the sea.

9
00:00:38,242 --> 00:00:44,281
And so the cycle goes on and on: the rain falling on you today could have been in the ocean yesterday!

10
00:00:44,281 --> 00:00:49,852
You can model it with warm water in a glass, covered with cling film and topped with ice cubes.

11
00:00:50,910 --> 00:00:54,370
A bowl of warm salty water has an empty cup in the middle.

12
00:00:54,370 --> 00:00:59,236
The bowl is covered with cling film, with an ice cube on top, right above the cup.

13
00:00:59,236 --> 00:01:03,751
Predict: will any water get into the cup? Will it be salty? Pause and decide.

14
00:01:04,810 --> 00:01:09,911
Watch. The bowl is left in the sun for an hour. Tiny drops appear under the cling film.

15
00:01:10,970 --> 00:01:16,774
The drops run to the lowest point and drip into the cup. The water in the cup does not taste salty.

16
00:01:17,833 --> 00:01:22,348
Explain what you saw. The warm water evaporated, but the salt stayed behind.

17
00:01:22,348 --> 00:01:26,804
The water vapour cooled under the cold cling film and condensed into drops,

18
00:01:26,804 --> 00:01:28,856
which fell like rain into the cup.

19
00:01:28,856 --> 00:01:33,312
This models evaporation, condensation and precipitation in the water cycle.

20
00:01:33,312 --> 00:01:35,599
Pause and explain it in your own words.

21
00:01:36,658 --> 00:01:42,111
Now it is your turn to shine! Pause the video after each question and try to answer it first.

22
00:01:43,169 --> 00:01:47,449
Question 1: Which layer of the Earth is the hottest? Pause the video now.

23
00:01:48,508 --> 00:01:49,857
Answer: The inner core.

24
00:01:50,915 --> 00:01:55,723
Question 2: What type of plate boundary forms fold mountains? Pause the video now.

25
00:01:56,782 --> 00:01:59,479
Answer: A convergent boundary, plates collide.

26
00:02:00,538 --> 00:02:04,525
Question 3: Which gas makes up most of the air? Pause the video now.

27
00:02:05,583 --> 00:02:07,636
Answer: Nitrogen, about 78 percent.

28
00:02:08,694 --> 00:02:14,968
Question 4: Name the process in which water vapour turns into droplets to form clouds. Pause the video now.

29
00:02:16,027 --> 00:02:17,258
Answer: Condensation.
